  "plain": "Apollo 11, the first mission to land people on the Moon, was launched on July 16, 1969, exactly 24 years after the Trinity test, the first atomic bomb test, which opened the nuclear age, and the timing is also tied to the astrological sign of Aquarius. Michels points this out himself, without naming a source, suggesting that if the date was chosen on purpose, the launch had a ritual meaning."
